\f0\fs24 \cf0 Add four secondary post-transplant outcomes to the harmonized GVHD metadata.\
\
Follow the "Harmonization Variable Additions" section of CLAUDE.md for all\
standing conventions.\
\
SHAPE: four binary covariates\
\
DEFINITION: Secondary post-transplant complications, recorded as simple 1/0\
event flags. No time-to-event columns and no severity columns for any of these \'97\
where a source records a grade, collapse it to presence/absence. Most are\
single-study; heavy NA is expected and fine.\
\
COLUMNS (all 1/0, all added to binary_outcome_cols):\
  myelosuppression          myelosuppression during the transplant course\
  mucositis                 mucositis (oral/GI) during the transplant course\
  bloodstream_infection     documented bacteraemia or fungaemia post-transplant\
  bronchiolitis_obliterans  bronchiolitis obliterans syndrome\
\
PLACEMENT: at the end of target_cols, after relapse_day_rel_transplant, in the\
order listed above. These are secondary outcomes and sit behind the primary\
GVHD, death and relapse blocks.\
\
PER-STUDY CONSTRUCTION:\
- Artacho:  Myelosuppression 0/1 -> myelosuppression (74 yes / 98 no).\
            Mucositis Yes/No -> mucositis (15 yes / 157 no).\
            Other new columns -> NA.\
- DAmico:   Mucositis_grade -> mucositis. Grades I, II and III -> 1. Both "/"\
            and NA -> 0, i.e. treat an ungraded patient as having no mucositis.\
            Expect 94 yes / 10 no.\
            BSI -> bloodstream_infection. The column is free text naming\
            organisms and days ("S.aureus (+7)"); any non-missing value -> 1,\
            NA -> 0. NA genuinely means no BSI here, confirmed by the manuscript\
            (all events were in the PN group; the EN group had zero). Expect\
            39 yes / 65 no.\
            Other new columns -> NA.\
- Fujimoto: not recorded -> NA for all four.\
- Ingham:   not recorded -> NA for all four.\
- Liu2017:  bloodstream_infection derived by READING the two free-text infection\
            fields. See the LIU BSI CLASSIFICATION section below.\
            Other new columns -> NA.\
- Vallet:   bos -> bronchiolitis_obliterans. "yes" -> 1; missing -> 0, NOT NA.\
            The dictionary states explicitly that NA/missing means no BOS, and\
            manuscript Table 1 reports BOS counts of 0, 0, 1, 1 by enterotype,\
            confirming exactly 2 cases. Expect 2 yes / 116 no.\
            Other new columns -> NA.\
\
LIU BSI CLASSIFICATION:\
Liu records infections as unstructured free text across two columns,\
infection_duringafter_transplant (45 distinct non-blank values among the 57\
recipients) and infection_details (27 distinct non-blank values). Do not write a\
regex. Instead:\
\
  1. Extract the complete list of distinct values from each column, restricted\
     to recipient rows.\
  2. Read every one of those ~72 strings and decide, per string, whether it\
     documents a bloodstream infection.\
     - Any documented bacteraemia counts as a BSI. If the text names bacteraemia\
       (however spelled, and including constructions like "CNS bacteremia",\
       "E coli bacteremia 12/2013", "bacteremia: pseudomonas, E coli, VRE"),\
       classify it 1.\
     - Fungaemia and candidaemia count as BSI.\
     - Non-bloodstream infections do not count: UTI, pneumonia, colitis,\
       cellulitis, sinusitis, abscess, oral candida, C difficile, and similar.\
     - Viral viremia (CMV, EBV, BK, adenovirus) does not count. BSI here means\
       bacteraemia or fungaemia.\
     - Organism names appearing without any site or bloodstream context are\
       ambiguous. Use your judgement, and list every call you were unsure about\
       in the decision log so I can review them.\
  3. Hard-code the resulting classification into harmonize_gvhd_metadata.R as an\
     explicit literal lookup: two named character vectors (or a small tibble)\
     mapping each distinct source string to 1 or 0. R cannot read free text at\
     runtime, so the reading happens once, now, and the code must contain the\
     finished crosswalk rather than a heuristic. Every distinct value must appear\
     in the lookup \'97 including the blank/NA value, which maps to 0.\
  4. A recipient is bloodstream_infection = 1 if EITHER column's value maps to 1.\
     Donor rows -> NA.\
  5. Add a QA table that reproduces the full crosswalk (source string, column,\
     classification, n samples) so the derivation stays auditable, and a test\
     asserting that every distinct source value in the real data is present in\
     the lookup \'97 so the script fails loudly rather than silently returning NA\
     if the source file ever changes.\
\
For reference, a strict regex on bacteremia|bacteraemia|fungemia|candidemia|\
septic shock|sepsis gives 13 of 57 recipients. Treat that as a sanity-check\
ballpark, not a target \'97 if your reading lands far from it, say why.\
\
NOTES:\
- Artacho's Myelosuppression belongs here, as its own outcome. If a conditioning\
  block already exists in the file, confirm Myelosuppression was NOT used to\
  populate conditioning_intensity \'97 it is a toxicity of conditioning, not a\
  description of it, and it should appear only in this new column.\
- Both mucositis sources carry a documented UNCERTAIN flag about the timing\
  window and severity threshold, and neither states its grading system. Artacho\
  is a bare Yes/No with no threshold given; DAmico uses an unnamed I/II/III\
  scale, and under the rule above an ungraded DAmico patient is treated as\
  mucositis-free rather than unknown. Pooling the two therefore compares two\
  undefined thresholds. Record that caveat in the log.\
- Six Liu recipients have both infection fields empty. They become 0, but "no\
  documented infection" and "not assessed" are not distinguishable in this\
  source. Note it; do not special-case them.\
- Ingham's tx_death is deliberately NOT harmonized. Do not add a\
  treatment_related_death column.\
\
Before editing anything, read the relevant study sheets in\
data_dictionaries.xlsx (the copy in Merging/, which is more current than the one\
in Merging/Harmonization/) and cross-tabulate the real source columns in the\
*_meta_qiime.tsv files. Then, before writing the Liu lookup into the script,\
show me your classification of the ~72 distinct infection strings as a table so\
I can review it. That is the one thing here I want to see before it lands.\
\
If the data contradicts the spec above, or you hit any of the stop-and-ask\
triggers in CLAUDE.md, stop and ask me. Otherwise proceed: edit\
harmonize_gvhd_metadata.R, extend build_qa() with a coverage row for each new\
column plus the Liu crosswalk table; add unit and end-to-end tests including the\
lookup-completeness assertion; run the test suite; and append an entry to\
to_log/harmonization_decisions.md recording the full Liu classification. Do not\
touch the xlsx.}